y\": true, \"majority_id\": \"server-5d6f41cb-8081-eeab-e638-6e9c72debee9\", \"majority_leader\": true, \"majority_log_has_entry\": true, \"minority_applied_len\": 16, \"minority_apply_ok\": false, \"minority_entry\": \"\", \"minority_fsm_has_entry\": false, \"minority_leader\": false, \"minority_log_has_entry\": false, \"mode\": \"div_off\", \"phase\": \"after_heal\", \"restore_committed_logs\": false, \"snapshots\": 1}\nCMP 0 violated witness [27] evaluated [27] complete True missing []\nCMP 1 holds witness [] evaluated [29] complete True missing []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"The agreement violation is witnessed: both sides acknowledged, and eight seconds after healing the two nodes hold different entries at the same index (control agrees). Finalizing."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"The last open point closed with a receipt. Receipt a608e5f60ae4415981c1024522a24a0d (exit 0, thirty events, no parse loss) resolves the agreement comparison as violated at witness event index 27: eight seconds after the partition healed, the isolated node and the majority-side leader hold different entries at the same log index (logs_differ_at_conflict_index true) while the same event records both_sides_acknowledged true and no node applied an entry absent from its own log; the flag-off control agrees at its index (comparison 1 holds, evaluated index 29). Together with the short-window negative from receipt 4e9eaa72cf594018b8414a8d8efb7cb3, the durability question is answered: the acknowledged entries are not lost from either log, but the two replicas permanently disagree at that index, each keeping the write its own client was told had succeeded. The question now has five complete violated comparisons with controls and one bounded negative; the interpretation is updated to cover them and the gap is resolved with the caveat that the compared entry payloads are not emitted, only the comparison derived from reading both logs.\\\")\nd['sources']=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":604,\\\"end_line\\\":620,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":724,\\\"end_line\\\":754,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":994,\\\"end_line\\\":1005,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":245,\\\"end_line\\\":275,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_requestvote_leader_guard\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1690,\\\"end_line\\\":1700,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1087,\\\"end_line\\\":1094,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1999,\\\"end_line\\\":2060,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_commit_recalc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"commitment.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":78,\\\"end_line\\\":104,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_log_matching\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1518,\\\"end_line\\\":1556,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\nd['knowledge']=[\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@log_disagreement_after_heal\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"When a node with a stale configuration won leadership on a minority of the committed configuration and both sides acknowledged a client write, the two nodes still held different entries at the same log index eight seconds after the partition healed, while neither node applied an entry absent from its own log; the flag-off control's two sides agreed at that index.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Five-voter committed configuration with a three-voter snapshot; RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a CommitTrackingLogStore; the restarted node isolated with one committed voter immediately after NewRaft returns and both sides acknowledging a distinct client write; eight second heal settle; in-memory log stores.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_log_matching\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"a608e5f60ae4415981c1024522a24a0d\\\":[27,29]}}\n]\nd.pop('experiment',None)\nd['interpretations']=[{\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"c1316acd314a48128d8dafe1d5be94e8-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_requestvote_leader_guard\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\",\\\"raft_commit_recalc\\\",\\\"raft_log_matching\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"a608e5f60ae4415981c1024522a24a0d\\\":[27,29],\\\"4e9eaa72cf594018b8414a8d8efb7cb3\\\":[27,29],\\\"f0db8b71047e42df96d3e2f4f581835c\\\":[27,29],\\\"abfdbd1823b342409ef4a815bade0407\\\":[21,22,24,25],\\\"b15f4b6c55b44402ace926204de9b826\\\":[15,18]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Five completed comparisons with controls establish the defect and its consequences, and one bounded negative marks its limit. Configuration: b15f4b6c55b44402ace926204de9b826, violated at witness event index 15 - the node restarted from a log whose latest configuration is index 14 with five servers came back at configuration index 1 with three servers - control holding at index 18. Election: abfdbd1823b342409ef4a815bade0407, violated at witness index 22 - the isolated node became leader with reachable_votes 2 against committed_quorum 3, with majority_side_leader also true - control holding at index 25. Single-side acknowledgement: 568bebb18e574cafa18e96add68e89db, violated at witness index 27 - the isolated leader's Apply completed - control holding at index 29. Two-sided acknowledgement: f0db8b71047e42df96d3e2f4f581835c, violated at witness index 27 - both sides acknowledged a client write concurrently - control holding at index 29. Log agreement after healing: a608e5f60ae4415981c1024522a24a0d, violated at witness index 27 - eight seconds after healing the isolated node and the majority-side leader hold different entries at the same log index while both_sides_acknowledged is true and neither node applied an entry absent from its own log - control holding at index 29 (the two sides agree). Limit: 4e9eaa72cf594018b8414a8d8efb7cb3 holds all three of its comparisons at the two-second window, so no loss or applied-without-log divergence occurred there, which is why the disagreement is reported as two logs keeping different entries rather than as a lost acknowledged entry. Source: restoreFromCommittedLogs (api.go:724-754) advances lastApplied to the persisted commit index before the startup scan at api.go:604-620, so AddVoter's later entry (api.go:994-1005) is never re-read and the node keeps the snapshot's three-server list; quorumSize() (raft.go:1087-1094) then returns two, electSelf (raft.go:1999-2060) asks only that list, and the commitment calculation (commitment.go:78-104) accepts two matching indexes, so leadership and acknowledgements rest on a majority of an obsolete configuration and the two sides never reconcile; the existing-leader vote guard (raft.go:1690-1700) is what makes the outcome schedule dependent, since the isolated side only wins when its single partner has also stopped hearing the majority leader.\\\",\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The flag-off controls in all six receipts keep the committed configuration, cannot win on the isolated side, do not acknowledge there and agree after healing.\\\",\\\"The two-second-window receipt is a negative for loss and for applied-without-log divergence, so the acknowledged entries are not shown to be lost, only to leave the two logs disagreeing.\\\",\\\"Two settled-schedule executions did not produce the minority leadership, explained by whether the isolated partner still heard the majority-side leader; no frequency or absence claim is made.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"Every observation is bounded (three second majority-leader wait, five second election window, two second apply timeout, two or eight second heal settle), so no occurrence-rate or absence bound is established.\\\",\\\"The agreement comparison is emitted as a derived boolean computed from reading both logs at the isolated side's last index; the two entry payloads themselves are not emitted, so what the entries contain is not inspectable from the receipt.\\\",\\\"The scenario restarts the former leader of a cluster grown by adding voters over in-memory stores; other roles, change types, chain orders and durable stores are not explored.\\\"],\n \\\"answers\\\":{\\\"7da03e78394f41fdad54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":False}}},\n }\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok-stage1')\nPYEOF\necho step1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
